+.. _tdcdft:
+
+tdcdft
+^^^^^^
+
+character, default='none'
+
+   | Experimental macroscopic xc vector potential, added to the PZ scalar potential.
+   | Options: ``'none'``, ``'lrc'``, ``'proca'``.
+   | In atomic units the normalized field a=Axc/c satisfies a'' + beta*a' + gamma*a = alpha*j,
+     where j is SALMON's volume-averaged electron-number current density.
+   | ``'lrc'`` requires beta=gamma=0. ``'proca'`` uses normalized alpha/beta/gamma (Williams and Ullrich, arXiv:2501.13290, Eq. 26); beta>=0.
+   | CPU only: theory='tddft_response' or 'tddft_pulse', periodic transverse response,
+     unpolarized PZ, fixed ions, middlepoint propagation, no symmetry reduction.
+   | Maxwell coupling, spin-orbit, DC, jellium, self-checkpoint and restart-time reset are unsupported.
+   | The classical field output is unchanged; the additional sysname_rt_xc.data contains Axc/c and Exc.
+   | RT restart requires tdcdft.bin with the same mode, time step and parameters.
+   | Fixed coefficients do not model carrier-dependent screening. Parameters require material-specific validation.
+
+.. _tdcdft_a2:
+
+tdcdft_a2
+^^^^^^^^^
+
+real(8), default=0d0
+
+   | Direct dimensionless Kohn-Sham-Proca coefficient (Dewhurst et al., PRB 111, L060302).
+   | With tdcdft='proca', set a finite nonzero a2 and supply tdcdft_a0.
+   | SALMON's opposite vector-potential sign gives alpha=-4*pi/a2 and restoring=a0/a2.
+   | Both signs of a2 are allowed; a0/a2 must be nonnegative.
+   | Do not mix direct coefficients with nonzero tdcdft_alpha or tdcdft_restoring.
+   | Si example in atomic units: tdcdft_a2=-85, tdcdft_a0=-0.2.
+
+.. _tdcdft_a0:
+
+tdcdft_a0
+^^^^^^^^^
+
+real(8), default=0d0
+
+   | Direct Proca mass-term coefficient, in inverse time squared (fs^-2 for A_eV_fs).
+   | a0=0 is allowed as a massless reference. The sign must agree with a2 otherwise.
+   | Requires (a0/a2)*dt**2<4; this bound does not guarantee coupled electronic stability.
+   | Optional tdcdft_damping remains a normalized inverse-time coefficient, not the paper's a1.
+   | Checkpoints store equivalent normalized coefficients; old normalized Proca input is still supported.
+
+.. _tdcdft_alpha:
+
+tdcdft_alpha
+^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+real(8), default=0d0
+
+   | Nonnegative dimensionless alpha for normalized input; derived alpha may be negative with direct positive a2.
+   | Zero removes the xc feedback. Enabled TDCDFT evaluates nonlocal current phases at the endpoint,
+     including at alpha=0; for time-dependent lasers use this enabled zero-coupling reference.
+
+.. _tdcdft_damping:
+
+tdcdft_damping
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+real(8), default=0d0
+
+   | Nonnegative beta. Input unit: inverse time (fs^-1 for unit_system='A_eV_fs').
+   | Available with tdcdft='proca'. This model damping is not a calibrated physical lifetime.
+
+.. _tdcdft_restoring:
+
+tdcdft_restoring
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+real(8), default=0d0
+
+   | Nonnegative gamma. Input unit: inverse time squared (fs^-2 for unit_system='A_eV_fs').
+   | Must be positive for normalized Proca input; direct a2/a0 also permits zero. Requires gamma*dt**2<4.
+   | This bound only concerns the uncoupled discrete oscillator, not full electronic stability.
+   | beta and gamma are logged after conversion to atomic units. They are normalized equation
+     coefficients. Optional tdcdft_a2 and tdcdft_a0 provide the Dewhurst parameterization.
+   | gamma introduces a low-frequency resonance and changes the frequency-dependent kernel.
+   | Validate stability and spectral sensitivity for the target material; 2D-model values are not Si presets.
+   | No instantaneous zero-force correction or automatic gamma threshold is implemented.
+
+.. _tdcdft_screening:
+
+tdcdft_screening and instantaneous-screening parameters
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+``tdcdft_screening``: character, default='none'; experimental options='instant', 'polarization', 'elf'.
+
+   | Instantaneous A,J,E,P estimator without time averaging. Only atomic-unit tddft_pulse input,
+     transverse periodic response, a non-impulse first pulse and normalized alpha are supported.
+   | Uses classical a=Ac_ext(t)-Ac_ext(0), E=-da/dt and integrated charge polarization P=-integral j dt.
+   | K=(a.j-E.P)/(a.a+E.E/omega**2); alpha_eff=alpha/[1+s*4*pi*max(K-K0,0)/omega**2].
+   | In 'instant' mode, the field acceleration is alpha_eff*j (plus optional damping/restoring).
+   | In 'polarization' mode, integrate a_xc'=-alpha_eff*P with second-order explicit stepping;
+     this mode requires beta=gamma=0 and removes the constant electric-field offset from changing alpha.
+   | The centered output field agrees with alpha_eff*P up to time-discretization errors during alpha changes.
+   | This is a phenomenological closure, not an inversion of the Drude dielectric function.
+   | tdcdft_screen_omega (real, default 0): positive representative angular frequency in atomic units.
+   | tdcdft_screen_reference (real, default 0): K0; calibrate with a weak laser at the same frequency.
+   | tdcdft_screen_strength (real, default 1): nonnegative s; zero gives fixed-alpha propagation and diagnostics.
+   | tdcdft_screen_floor (real, default 1e-8): positive threshold for sqrt(a.a+E.E/omega**2), in A/c units.
+   | Below the threshold, K and alpha are held; P continues to evolve. Pulse tails with residual P can
+     contaminate K before this threshold, so check threshold sensitivity before physical interpretation.
+   | Extra rt_xc.data columns are alpha_eff, K and P_xyz, all in atomic units.
+   | Version-2 checkpoints preserve the screening state. Version-1 files support fixed screening only.
+   | Weak-response recovery requires calibration; strong-field accuracy and stability are not established.
+
+
+ELF-dependent alpha
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+   | ``tdcdft_screening='elf'`` uses Q=integral n*(ELF-1/2)^2 / integral n and alpha=alpha0*Q/Q_initial.
+   | Requires tdcdft='lrc' in atomic units. Both pulse and impulse calculations are supported.
+   | ``tdcdft_elf_stride`` (integer, default10) evaluates current-corrected ELF every this many steps.
+   | Q_initial is measured from the initial state; alpha is held between evaluations, without time averaging.
+   | Native finite-difference Bloch gradients, occupation/k weights and summed local orbital current are used.
+   | Alpha starts at alpha0 and vanishes at the continuum cold uniform-gas ELF=1/2 limit; no upper clipping.
+   | This is an empirical localization closure, not a dielectric derivation or proof of metallic transport.
+   | Integrates a_xc'=-alpha*P with held alpha; damping and restoring must be zero.
+   | No external-field threshold is used. Existing tdcdft_screen_stop can freeze Q after a specified time.
+   | The 13 output columns are time, a_xc_xyz, E_xc_xyz, alpha, Q, P_xyz and Q_initial.
+   | ELF restart requires version4 and matching stride; old modes remain compatible with their old checkpoints.
+   | Q_initial<=1e-14 is rejected because normalization is undefined. See the ELF-feedback validation record.
+
